  "rationale": "Both translations correctly denote urine, and the anatomical sense is correct. However, the relation \"different-common-word\" is misleading as a national contrast: \"air kencing\" is also a valid Indonesian term, while \"air seni\" is recognized in Malay as a synonym. The card should present these as overlapping synonyms, with possible register or preference differences rather than a clean Indonesian-versus-Malaysian split.",
  "claim_reviews": [
    {
      "subject": "English cue and sense",
      "conclusion": "Correct: urine is liquid excreted by the kidneys and stored in the bladder before excretion.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=206468&keyword=air+kencing",
        "https://kbbi.web.id/urine"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "Indonesian answer: air seni",
      "conclusion": "Correct and natural; Indonesian dictionaries define \"air seni\" as \"air kencing\".",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://baru.kbbi.co.id/arti-kata/air%2Bseni",
        "https://kbbi.web.id/urine"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "Malaysian answer: air kencing",
      "conclusion": "Correct and standard Malay; PRPM defines it as urine.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=206468&keyword=air+kencing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "Final relation: different-common-word",
      "conclusion": "Misleading. The forms overlap across Indonesian and Malaysian Malay, so this should not be taught as an exclusive national distinction.",
      "material_risk": true,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://kbbi.co.id/arti-kata/air%2Bkencing",
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=73980&keyword=seni+II+1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "False-friend contrast",
      "conclusion": "No false-friend contrast is supported. The relevant issue is synonym overlap and possible register or preference variation, not divergent meaning.",
      "material_risk": true,
      "evidence_limitation": "The cited dictionary entries establish synonymy but do not independently quantify regional frequency or register preference."
    }
  ]
}
